      "title": "feat: add nine-key Pinyin input with syllable selection",
      "body": "Provide a complete nine-key input path using the existing luna_pinyin dictionary.\nKeep syllable locks, undo, raw-code edits and literal digits on the Rime dispatcher,\nand ship the matching layouts, spelling panel and revision-bound actions.\n\nPreserve batched Hanzi candidates and map displayed caret positions to native input.\nHandle standard UTF-8 through the JNI bridge so supplementary characters and offsets\nremain consistent. Keep symbol category input in Chinese mode and literal pages explicit.\n\nInclude focused native, controller, protocol and theme regressions. Keep prediction,\nprivacy policy, candidate pinning and fork release configuration outside this feature.\n\nRelated: #1464, #1299, #459",
      "conventional": true,
      "body_characters": 703,
